    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical approach for designing a prompt regression test for local LLMs. The objective is to compare the performance of an old prompt set against a new one using a consistent model configuration.\n\nWe start with a fixed set of 12 test prompts (F1). This set is designed to cover both scenarios where answers are expected and cases where the provided information is insufficient for a definitive response (F3). The core of the test involves running both the old and new prompt versions through the same model, ensuring all other model settings remain identical (F2). This controlled comparison aims to isolate the impact of prompt changes.\n\nIt is crucial to note that this is a hypothetical experiment brief. No actual results or measurements have been obtained yet (F4). The focus is purely on the methodology for setting up such a test. Further discussion is invited on refining this testing framework, particularly regarding the systematic evaluation of prompt effectiveness across diverse query types.",
